{
  "name": "Make product images in bulk from a Google Sheet with Nano Banana 2 and Z-Image (MartLLM)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Make product images in bulk from a Google Sheet\n\nEach row of your sheet becomes one image. The image is saved to your Google Drive, and its link, what it cost and whether it worked are written back to the same row.\n\n### Your sheet\nFirst row = column names, lower case:\n- `prompt` (needed): what the image should show.\n- `product` (optional): used as the file name.\n- `photo_link` (optional): a public `https://` link to a real photo of the product. With a photo, the product in the image is your real product. Without one, the image is made from the prompt alone.\n\nThe workflow adds `image_link`, `cost_usd` and `status` by itself. A row is made when `prompt` is filled and `image_link` is empty, so you can run it again and again: finished rows are skipped, failed rows are tried again.\n\n### Set up (5 minutes)\n1. Get an API key at [martllm.com](https://martllm.com/go/n8n-bulk-product-images) and add credit.\n2. Open **Make the image** → Credential → Create new → **Header Auth**:\n   - Name: `Authorization`\n   - Value: `Bearer ` followed by your key\n   The other MartLLM steps use the same credential. If you already made it for another MartLLM or UberLLM template, pick that one.\n3. Open **Read the sheet** and **Write the row back**: connect Google Sheets, then pick your spreadsheet and tab in both.\n4. Open **Save to Google Drive**: connect Google Drive and pick a folder.\n5. Click **Execute workflow**.\n\n### Price\nListed on 2026-11-25: $0.0042 per image from a prompt (Z-Image Turbo), $0.0165 per image from a product photo (Nano Banana 2). Prices move: [live prices](https://martllm.com/models).\n\n### What you pay\n- Each request costs what the seller that made it charged. No MartLLM fee on requests.\n- Anything that is not made costs nothing.\n- Adding credit by card costs 5.5% + $0.50. Credit does not expire while your account is open.\n",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "d934dda8-3a2b-5efc-92fd-7164ccceebec",
      "name": "Note: start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Change it here\n**Settings** holds the two models, the shape (`square`, `portrait` or `landscape`), words added to every prompt, how many rows one run may make, and the most one image may cost.\n\nAny image model on [martllm.com/models](https://martllm.com/models) works: copy its id.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "00ce4087-8421-56ff-bcea-9ce6f9185c40",
      "name": "Note: settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### One row at a time\nA row that cannot be made does not stop the others. The reason the API gave is written in the row's `status` cell, nothing is charged for it, and the next run tries it again.",
        "height": 150,
        "width": 900,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "71a9ceb0-a9b9-5b50-81eb-3ed0eb54ccd7",
      "name": "Note: one row at a time",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
